{
    "background_story": "Isaias was a young apprentice to the legendary Sir Thomas Malory, the renowned author of Le Morte d'Arthur. Growing up in 15th-century England, Isaias was fascinated by the tales of King Arthur and the Knights of the Round Table. Under Malory's guidance, he learned the art of storytelling and the intricacies of chivalry. As Malory's health began to decline, Isaias became his trusted scribe, helping to complete the manuscript of Le Morte d'Arthur. Isaias's dedication and passion for the story ensured that Malory's masterpiece would be preserved for generations to come. After Malory's passing, Isaias continued to share the tales of Arthurian legend with the world, keeping the spirit of his mentor alive.",
